### A PREVIEW campaign end to end, as an operator who is a member of the campaign's queue.
### 1. Create the campaign and add targets as an admin (campaign.http — "Create Operator Campaign"),
###    then start it: POST /api/campaigns/{id}/start

### 2. Take the next card (or the one already held). data = null: nobody is due now.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/operator/campaigns/1/next
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_token}}

### 3. Dial it — the operator's softphone rings first, then the client is dialled
POST http://localhost:8080/api/operator/campaigns/1/targets/10/dial
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_token}}

### 3b. ...or put it back without dialling (due again in 15 minutes)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/operator/campaigns/1/targets/10/skip
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_token}}

### 4. After the conversation: close the call. Its id is the card's callId — call next again once
###    the client is dialled; the same card comes back, now with callId set.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/calls/42/wrap-up
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_token}}

{
  "wrapUpCodeId": 1
}
